CORE
nested_call1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r0 == 4'b1010: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.r1 == 4'b1100: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.r2 == 4'b1000: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p3\] always \(##1 main\.q == 4'b1011\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A call of a function as an argument of another call of the same function.
The parameters of the function are assigned when expanding the inner call,
which must not clobber the arguments of the outer call.
